&lt;/p&gt;

---

Rondo is now a firmware for the Innioasis Y1: the Y1 starts straight into Rondo&#x27;s click-wheel menus, with nothing else on it.

**For the Y1, Type A only** (players that shipped with software 2.0.0 or later). Not for the Type B or the Y2.

## Install

Choose **Rondo** in [Innioasis Updater CE](https://innioasis.app) (Y1, Type A). Or download `rom.zip` below and use the Updater&#x27;s **Settings › Install from a file…**.

Installing replaces everything on the Y1 itself: the original player, Rockbox, settings. **The microSD card isn&#x27;t touched**, so your music stays. When the Updater is done, press the Y1&#x27;s Power button; the first start takes a couple of minutes. The [install guide](https://github.com/jarvissax/rondo/blob/main/docs/install.md) has the details and the first steps after it.

For YouTube Music and YouTube, [set up a Rondo server](https://github.com/jarvissax/rondo/blob/main/docs/server.md) with Docker, at home or on a VPS.

## Updates

Later versions install over this one in a minute, without flashing again, keeping your settings, Wi-Fi, playlists and music: **Settings › Software update** on the Y1, **Install** in the dashboard, or [the update page](https://jarvissax.github.io/rondo/) over USB.

## What&#x27;s in it

- iPod-style menus for the click wheel, with optional vibration and a click on every step
- Your music and videos from the microSD card, with covers, lyrics, search and playlists
- The card as a USB drive when the Y1 is plugged into a computer
- YouTube Music and YouTube, streamed live through your own server, including Shorts, with or without a YouTube account
- FM radio with station names, scanning and saved stations
- Bluetooth headphones and speakers, and Wi-Fi, set up from the wheel
- A dashboard in your phone&#x27;s browser for music, playlists, settings, the theme, Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, the radio and updates
- Shut down and restart from Settings, or by holding the Power button

## Good to know

- Only the Y1 Type A is supported; the Type B and Y2 haven&#x27;t been tested.
- Rockbox, the original player and Android&#x27;s own Settings aren&#x27;t part of Rondo. Innioasis Updater CE puts any of them back.
- YouTube Music and YouTube need your own Rondo server; the card, the radio and Bluetooth don&#x27;t.

